Z||000006||Master_Sushi||11-29-2001||01:15 PM||||Ok, I might sound like an idiot. But isnt that blue thing the oil filter? If so, whys it on the engine?<P>Oh and good luck with the install!||||reg||1
Z||000007||BlackStang95||11-29-2001||01:23 PM||||You put the filter on during engine building to stop oil from leaking out and to not get paint on the oil filter seal (where it connects to the engine) when you paint the block.||||reg||1
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||11-29-2001||01:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>You put the filter on during engine building to stop oil from leaking out and to not get paint on the oil filter seal (where it connects to the engine) when you paint the block.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><B>YUP!</B> That's why the filter is also half-red  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||11-30-2001||07:50 PM||||That engine will never work!  The Cylinders are facing the down instead of up.  All motors that go in Fieros have to have the cylinders facing upward.  Doh!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> <BR>"And this one time, on the Fiero Forum..."||||reg||1
